course: dictionary
lesson: 6285
title: Monthly, once a month
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Monthly means once every month. The word comes from «month», so it tells you how often something happens. «My pocket money is paid monthly.» That means it arrives once a month, not every week.
explain: Monthly can also mean measured over one whole month. «The town recorded its monthly rainfall.» Ask yourself: how often, or over how long? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Monthly can work as more than one kind of word. «We have a monthly meeting.» (adjective) «The club meets monthly.» (adverb) «Dad reads a monthly about cars.» (noun: a magazine that comes out once a month). The words around it tell you which one it is.
fact: Monthly means once every month.
fact: Some months have 4 weeks and some have 5, so money paid weekly does not always add up to the same as money paid monthly.
fact: To find a yearly total from a monthly amount, multiply by 12, because there are 12 months in a year.
fact: «Small monthly subscriptions add up to big amounts over a year.» It is worth checking them now and then.
fact: A monthly is a noun for a magazine that comes out once a month.
exercise: «My club meets monthly, on the first Saturday.» What does monthly mean here? | *Once every month | Measured over one week | Every single day | Only in the summer
exercise: Why might weekly pay not always match monthly pay? | *Some months have 5 weeks and some have 4 | Money is never paid weekly | Monthly means every day | Weeks are longer than months
exercise: Ali gets £5 pocket money monthly. How much does he get in a whole year? | £17 | *£60 | £12 | £500
test: «The school magazine is a monthly.» What kind of word is monthly here? | An adverb, meaning once a month | *A noun, a magazine that comes out once a month | An adjective, meaning very old | A verb, meaning to count the months
test: «The town recorded its monthly rainfall.» Which phrase means the same as monthly here? | Very heavy | Every hour | *Measured over one month | Only on Sundays
exam: Which sentence uses monthly to mean happening once every month? | Our monthly is on the shelf. | The monthly rainfall was high. | Monthly has seven letters. | *We pay the club fee monthly.
